--- a/docs/user/limitations.md
+++ b/docs/user/limitations.md
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ Stated plainly so that nothing here is mistaken for a claim.
 - **No performance numbers are published with this release.** Numbers elsewhere in the repository are debug-build, loopback, single-host or simulated; none is a release-grade measurement.
 - **Serving model.** GET is served from the local cache only; there is no cross-gateway read-through.
 - **Cluster mode is experimental.** In the mTLS cluster configuration the local cluster node shares the gateway's HTTP serving cache, so invalidation frames received from peers purge it (`src/main.rs:327`); GET is still served from the local cache only. An anti-entropy reconciliation worker runs every 250 ms in cluster configurations (`src/main.rs:370`, `:378`); its effectiveness is not established. The insecure/partial cluster configuration (`PHANTOM_ALLOW_INSECURE_CLUSTER` without full mTLS material) has no peer addresses: no invalidation frame is sent or received, and DELETE returns a gateway timeout (`src/main.rs:376`). Membership is static. See "Cluster invalidation durability" below.
-- **Staleness.** Entries expire by origin headers (`s-maxage`, `max-age`, `Expires`) or, when the origin gives none, a fixed 60 s default (`PHANTOM_DEFAULT_TTL_MS` is validated but not honored: `src/config.rs:116-117`, literal `60_000` at `src/api/server.rs:1367` and `:1650`). **Origin-supplied lifetimes have no gateway ceiling** (`src/core/freshness.rs:263-276`), and the hard stale cap `PHANTOM_MAX_STALE_MS` limits only how long an expired entry may be served stale (stale-while-revalidate / stale-if-error), not the freshness lifetime. No linearizability or bounded-staleness guarantee beyond that is claimed.
+- **Staleness.** Entries expire by origin headers (`s-maxage`, `max-age`, `Expires`) or, when the origin gives none, `PHANTOM_DEFAULT_TTL_MS` (default 60 s; applied by `main` via `api::server::set_default_ttl_ms`). **Origin-supplied lifetimes have no gateway ceiling** (`src/core/freshness.rs:263-276`), and the hard stale cap `PHANTOM_MAX_STALE_MS` limits only how long an expired entry may be served stale (stale-while-revalidate / stale-if-error), not the freshness lifetime. No linearizability or bounded-staleness guarantee beyond that is claimed.
 - **Dashboard.** Parts of the SSE stream and UI are synthetic when `PHANTOM_SIMULATION=true`; simulated values are labeled and are not measurements.
 - **Shutdown.** No in-flight connection draining yet (see operate.md), and no drain of pending cluster invalidations (`src/main.rs:484-490`; see "Cluster invalidation durability" below).
 - **Idle CPU.** The lazy-reclamation sweeper task is started with a shutdown channel whose sender is dropped immediately. An idle process was observed using more than one core of CPU (single runs: debug build about 6.5 CPU-seconds in about 5 s wall; release build 14.8 CPU-seconds in 10 s wall, Windows 11, loopback, no traffic). The probable cause (a `watch::changed()` that is always ready in the select loop) was identified by code reading and has not been isolated experimentally; only single runs exist (no repetitions or intervals).
